  <constraints>
    <constraint type="cost">Epic compilation is heavier than story compilation (~$0.10-0.20 per run vs. ~$0.03-0.08). The COMPILER agent must read and reason across ALL articles touched by the epic. Optimize prompt to minimize token usage.</constraint>
    <constraint type="non-blocking">Epic compilation failure MUST NOT revert the epic's completed status. The app is already built — compilation is post-processing knowledge synthesis.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">This story depends on Epic 2 being complete. Story compilation pipeline must be operational so individual story articles exist for the epic compiler to synthesize.</constraint>
    <constraint type="ordering">The agent step (consolidate) must complete BEFORE the shell step (graph-resync). Supersession marking and maturity updates must be written to wiki files before Memgraph sync.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Wiki markdown files are the source of truth. Memgraph is a disposable query accelerator rebuilt from wiki content. The COMPILER agent writes to wiki files; graph-sync reads wiki files and upserts to Memgraph.</constraint>
    <constraint type="status-lifecycle">The supersession scan handles active -> superseded transitions ONLY. Pruning (superseded -> pruned, moving to archive/) is handled by Story 3.4 after deployment.</constraint>
  </constraints>

